  "validity_note": "Laliberte (2009) aqueous-electrolyte correlation for Ca(NO3)2-water, density and viscosity. Tabulated for 2-40 wt% over 25-60 degC. The 25 degC floor is the lower bound of the correlation's Ca(NO3)2 density data (fitted 25-60 degC); the table is not extrapolated below it. Heat capacity is not tabulated (the correlation carries no Ca(NO3)2 heat-capacity coefficients). Calcium nitrate is very soluble (above 50 wt% at 25 degC), so the 40 wt% ceiling stays below saturation. Concentrations are anhydrous Ca(NO3)2 by mass; the common tetrahydrate is about 78% Ca(NO3)2 by mass. Values are for preliminary design; verify against vendor data for critical service.",
